     [38;5;246mBell/inbox in the app as the durable record, email for reach when people aren't looking. Channel-agnostic delivery
[39m     [38;5;246mlayer so push can be added later without rework. Adds one external dependency (a mail sender).[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m In-app only
     [38;5;246mBell icon and notification inbox, nothing else. Zero external dependencies, nothing to configure, fastest to ship.
[39m     [38;5;246mBut people only find out when they happen to open the app.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m In-app + email + push
     [38;5;246mEverything, including browser push. Best reach, but service workers, permission prompts, and per-browser behavior [39m
     [38;5;246mare a meaningful chunk of work for a desk-bound internal team.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Email only
     [38;5;246mNo in-app inbox; everything goes to the mail client where people already live. Simple mental model, but there's no
